# Git applies the LAST matching pattern, so INCLUDE rules come first and the
# narrower IGNORE rules below them win. Un-ignoring the directory itself before
# its contents matters: git will not descend into an excluded directory, so
# `!.planning/**` alone cannot rescue files if a host repo ignored `.planning/`
# or used a broad `.*` rule.

# --- INCLUDE: the shared team brain. This MUST travel with the repo. ---
!.comind/
!.comind/manifest.json
!.planning/
!.planning/**
!.ai-memory/
!.ai-memory/**
!.claude/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/**
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/**
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/agents/**
# The GSD engine itself. Without it a clone gets gsd-* slash commands pointing
# at nothing, and JOIN will not reinstall — gsd-core writes committed files, so
# only FIRST INIT may run it. The /** line also rescues .gsd-runtime from a host
# repo's `.*` rule, since the last matching pattern wins.
#
# scripts/ is part of the engine, not an extra: gsd-core/bin/lib does
# `require('../../../scripts/…')`, so a clone without it gets MODULE_NOT_FOUND
# from gsd-tools.cjs. package.json is `{"type":"commonjs"}` and is what lets
# gsd-core's .js hooks load in a repo whose own package.json is type:module.
!.claude/gsd-core/
!.claude/gsd-core/**
!.claude/scripts/
!.claude/scripts/**
!.claude/package.json
!.claude/gsd-file-manifest.json
!.gitattributes

# --- IGNORE: machine-local, derived, or regenerated on clone ---

# graphify. Upstream ships graphify-out/ to be COMMITTED — "so everyone on the
# team starts with a map" — and a clone that lacks graph.json cannot answer
# `/gsd-graphify query` at all; it has to pay for a full extraction first.
#
# This section reads ignore-then-negate, the opposite of the file's overall
# order, because git will not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY: `graphify-out/`
# followed by negations rescues nothing. Excluding the entries (`/*`) and
# re-including the five that matter is the only spelling that works.
#
# Committed: graph.json is the queryable substrate. The two dotfile sidecars are
# LLM output — .graphify_labels.json holds the generated community names, and
# `graphify export html` reads them ONLY from there, never from the
# `community_name` attribute graph.json also carries. Drop it and every
# teammate's viz degrades to "Community 0" and re-pays for labelling on rebuild.
#
# Excluded: graph.html is a pure local render of the files above — zero API
# cost, regenerated by /comind-sync — and it is the largest, churniest artifact
# with no merge driver behind it. cost.json, cache/, memory/ and the pinned
# interpreter path are machine-local by upstream's own guidance.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/graph.json
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!graphify-out/manifest.json
!graphify-out/.graphify_labels.json
!graphify-out/.graphify_analysis.json

# Per-developer overrides. gsd-core writes its own hooks here, and they embed
# this machine's absolute node path — never shareable.
.claude/settings.local.json
# gsd-core's migration log, stamped with this machine's clock on every run.
.claude/gsd-install-state.json

# RTK writes RTK.md and its hook to ~/.claude, not the repo. Nothing to ignore
# here; each developer gets it from `rtk init -g` via `comind setup` (/comind-init).

# CoMind machine-local state. The rtk binary and the download cache are NOT
# here — they live in ~/.claude/comind/, outside every repo, so no clone can
# ship a binary CoMind would then execute.
.comind/state/

# Obsidian per-user UI state. The shared .obsidian/app.json stays included above.
.ai-memory/.obsidian/workspace*.json
.ai-memory/.obsidian/cache
.ai-memory/.obsidian/plugins/

# Scratch notes a developer wants kept out of the shared brain.
.planning/**/*.local.md

# RTK local savings metrics.
.rtk/
